{"id":"annapurna-circuit","title":"Annapurna Circuit","who":"Classic route · round the Annapurna massif","when":"Best October–November and March–May","vehicle":"On foot, 10–16 days, teahouses","kind":"walk","color":"#9333ea","summary":"From the green Marsyangdi valley up through Buddhist villages to Manang, over the Thorong La pass at 5,416 m and down to the pilgrimage temples of Muktinath and the deep Kali Gandaki gorge. Teahouses all the way; the acclimatisation days in Manang matter.","sources":[{"label":"Dave's Travel Corner: Annapurna Circuit journal (July 2025)","url":"https://www.davestravelcorner.com/?p=139934"},{"label":"Explore-Share: 11-day itinerary, lodges and food","url":"https://www.explore-share.com/blog/annapurna-circuit-eleven-day-itinerary-route-lodges-food/"}],"approximate":"The usual stages anticlockwise; the line follows trails and jeep tracks near the route.","km":242,"bbox":[83.5948,28.231,84.4144,28.8412],"stops":[{"name":"Besisahar","place":"Besisahar, Nepal","at":[28.2313,84.3761],"text":"The start, after a long bus ride from Kathmandu. Many now jeep further up to skip the road.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Besi_Sahar.JPG/500px-Besi_Sahar.JPG","page":"Besishahar","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Besi_Sahar.JPG","credit":"Dmitry A. Mottl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Chame","place":"Chame, Nepal","at":[28.5507,84.2424],"text":"Up the Marsyangdi gorge past waterfalls into pine forest, Annapurna II above."},{"name":"Pisang","place":"Upper Pisang, Nepal","at":[28.6164,84.153],"text":"Into the dry rain shadow: stone villages, prayer flags and the curved rock face of Paungda Danda.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Upper_and_Lower_Pisang.jpg/500px-Upper_and_Lower_Pisang.jpg","page":"Pisang","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Upper_and_Lower_Pisang.jpg","credit":"Kondephy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Manang","place":"Manang, Nepal","at":[28.6667,84.0167],"text":"Two nights at 3,540 m to acclimatise, with side hikes to the Gangapurna glacier lake or Ice Lake."},{"name":"Yak Kharka","place":"Yak Kharka, Nepal","at":[28.7227,83.9738],"text":"Short days now, climbing slowly above the tree line.","source":{"label":"Dave's Travel Corner (2025)","url":"https://www.davestravelcorner.com/?p=139934"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Annapurna%2C_Manang_District.jpg/500px-Annapurna%2C_Manang_District.jpg","page":"Manang District, Nepal","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Annapurna%2C_Manang_District.jpg","credit":"Poida Smith","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Thorong Phedi","place":"Thorong Phedi, Nepal","at":[28.7768,83.9726],"text":"The last lodges below the pass, about 4,500 m. An early night and a very early start.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Muktinath_Valley%2C_View_of_Thorong_La_Pass%2C_Mountains%2C_Nepal.jpg/500px-Muktinath_Valley%2C_View_of_Thorong_La_Pass%2C_Mountains%2C_Nepal.jpg","page":"Thorong La","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Muktinath_Valley%2C_View_of_Thorong_La_Pass%2C_Mountains%2C_Nepal.jpg","credit":"Vyacheslav Argenberg","license":"CC BY 4.0"}},{"name":"Thorong La","place":"Thorong La","at":[28.7936,83.9381],"text":"The pass at 5,416 m, usually crossed before sunrise winds.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Muktinath_Valley%2C_View_of_Thorong_La_Pass%2C_Mountains%2C_Nepal.jpg/500px-Muktinath_Valley%2C_View_of_Thorong_La_Pass%2C_Mountains%2C_Nepal.jpg","page":"Thorong La","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Muktinath_Valley%2C_View_of_Thorong_La_Pass%2C_Mountains%2C_Nepal.jpg","credit":"Vyacheslav Argenberg","license":"CC BY 4.0"}},{"name":"Muktinath","place":"Muktinath, Nepal","at":[28.8167,83.8711],"text":"A long descent to a temple sacred to both Hindus and Buddhists.","source":{"label":"Explore-Share itinerary","url":"https://www.explore-share.com/blog/annapurna-circuit-eleven-day-itinerary-route-lodges-food/"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/The_Muktinath_Temple.jpg/500px-The_Muktinath_Temple.jpg","page":"Muktinath","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Muktinath_Temple.jpg","credit":"Ironicfreak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Marpha","place":"Marpha, Nepal","at":[28.7519,83.6862],"text":"Down the windy Kali Gandaki to a whitewashed village famous for apple brandy.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Marpha%2CMustang%2CNepal.jpg/500px-Marpha%2CMustang%2CNepal.jpg","page":"Marpha","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marpha%2CMustang%2CNepal.jpg","credit":"Saddam19","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Tatopani","place":"Tatopani, Myagdi","at":[28.4875,83.6531],"text":"Hot springs at the bottom of one of the world's deepest gorges."},{"name":"Poon Hill","place":"Ghorepani, Nepal","at":[28.4025,83.6999],"text":"A sunrise over Dhaulagiri and Annapurna, a favourite finale.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Poon_hill_sunrise.jpg/500px-Poon_hill_sunrise.jpg","page":"Poon Hill","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Poon_hill_sunrise.jpg","credit":"Thapaliyashreeram","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Nayapul","place":"Nayapul, Nepal","at":[28.2981,83.7679],"text":"Down to the road and on to Pokhara and its lake.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Pokhara_Valley.jpg/500px-Pokhara_Valley.jpg","page":"Pokhara","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pokhara_Valley.jpg","credit":"Utsab Raj Giri","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}],"legs":[{"by":"walk","km":59,"line":[[28.231,84.3762],[28.2364,84.3712],[28.2411,84.3753],[28.2849,84.3641],[28.3109,84.401],[28.327,84.4007],[28.3367,84.4075],[28.3521,84.4085],[28.3901,84.4021],[28.4089,84.4144],[28.426,84.3